I had a decent start on a gnome wizard.  I had found a very large
general store, and while it didn't yield any spectacular equipment it
did provide about four scrolls of identify.  But even then I was
struggling to survive since that particular store only had one mimic
and it was a giant.  Luckily, my little gnome had been born with a wand
of teleport and after paying my tab I teleported myself away from that
nasty mimic.  I found an altar around level 4 and managed to convert it
and eventually sacrifice enough for magic bane.  My exp level had risen
up to 7 or 8 by then though and that was giving me some concern but I
figured that since I had Magicbane I'd get by with a whole bunch of E
words.  During this time, I had been knocked off the altar a few times
by monsters, once by a swarm of bees, once by a pack(?) of rothes.  I
was surviving by the skin of my teeth before I got Magicbane.

I chose to head down to minetown since I was a gnome I figured the
mines would be relatively easy and maybe I'd catch a wish to lower my
AC.  The first level of the mines provided me with a pair of bugbears
right by the stairs.  A couple of trips back up the stairs to regain
health gave me enough power to shoot them down.  A few steps away and I
spotted several green elves.  Now I know I was in trouble considering
their disdain for the E-Word.  They managed to get between me and the
steps and suddenly I'm down to 4 hps with them hitting me along with
another monster or two.  I used my last charge of teleport wand to get
away.  I'm free and clear, but I can't pray since I had prayed
recently, so my hope was to get some clear shots on them and maybe run
around them to get to the up stairs.

Two steps later, you fall into a spiked pit!  You Die!  DYWYPI?

Talk about an anti-climax.  Those poor elves were robbed of their kill
by a spiked pit.  And it wasn't even a poisoned one.



